Overlay patch 0021 (rev7: async shader compilation [D-008, gSohIos.AsyncShaders, DEFAULT ON — device+user validated; cvar ...0 to disable] + draw-skip guard; rev6: +shader-library compile ledger; rev5: +per-window PSO ledger; rev4: +PSO-compile ledger — folded here per D6,
the atomics block adjoins rev3's upload ledger): Metal texture memory
safety + mip engine + GPU frame-time export. rev1: dim clamp (Metal aborts
past the device limit; OOB-fallback strips), newTexture nil-guard, byte
ledger, working DeleteTexture (upstream's was EMPTY), LRU byte-budget
eviction (gSohIos.TexCacheBudgetMB, default 1536, floor 128 entries).
rev2 (reference 0019 rev3+rev4, 0020 rev2, 0028):
- Mip chains for >=256px textures — single-level minification of 2048px+
  pack textures was a bandwidth catastrophe (reference: 31 ms GPU frames in
  vistas; 3.8 ms with mips).
- Mip generation DEFERRED to ONE EndFrame blit pass on the frame's own
  command buffer — per-upload mid-frame command buffers queue behind the
  enqueue()d frame CB and deadlock past ~63 uploads/frame (reference Hyrule
  Field freeze, music still playing). Non-optional discipline.
- Ledger is mip-aware on all add/subtract sites (+1/3 for a chain).
- True GPU frame time (gSohIosGpuMs, shell-defined) via a completed
  handler on the screen command buffer — in THIS patch because my fork's
  compact EndFrame puts the blit and the handler 2 lines apart (one hunk
  region = one patch, D6); the probe (0008 rev4) and the bridge's
  `drawable` command read it. Extern is FILE-scope (block-scope linkage
  specs don't compile in C++ — reference trap).
rev3 (stutter round 3): aggregate UploadTexture CPU time + count per perf
window into atomics (SohIos_UploadStats, read by 0008 rev7 as up_ms/ups).
Round 2 convicted transitions but timed loads covered only ~10% of the
stall — the first-draw upload burst (replaceRegion memcpy on the game
thread) is the prime suspect for the rest, and this is the instrument the
Vision Pro 4K ladder needs regardless.

